<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Supayalat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1859–1925</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Supayalat was the last queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, the daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindon-min">King Mindon</a> and Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hsinbyumashin">Hsinbyumashin</a> and the wife of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thibaw-min">Thibaw</a>, her half-brother. She dominated Thibaw's court and is held responsible, with her mother's faction, for the massacre of royal relatives in 1879. After the British conquest of 1885 she went into exile with Thibaw at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratnagiri">Ratnagiri</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, returning to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangon">Rangoon</a> after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/supayalat.jpg" alt="Supayalat" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Queen_Supayalat_of_Burma.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
